<main class="demo-shell">
    <nav class="demo-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <wa-breadcrumb label="Page navigation">
            <wa-breadcrumb-item href="./">Home</wa-breadcrumb-item>
            <wa-breadcrumb-item aria-current="page">Timeline demo</wa-breadcrumb-item>
        </wa-breadcrumb>
    </nav>

    <header class="demo-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">@lgs1920/timeline vx.y.z</p>
        <h1>A timeline you can shape.</h1>
        <p class="intro">Explore the component through focused examples: a Studio-style controlled timeline, external time and zoom sliders, read-only rendering, range editing, slots, and event-driven updates.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="demo-panel playground studio-demo" aria-labelledby="studio-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Demo 01 · Studio integration</p>
                <h2 id="studio-title">Control the timeline from the host</h2>
            </div>
            <span id="studio-status" class="event-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</span>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">The timeline stays controlled by its host. The standard time and zoom controls remain inside the component. The play button emits a playback intent, then the host clock advances <code>currentTimeMillis</code>. The host adds 10-second seek actions through the top menu slot.</p>
        <div class="clip-source-panel" aria-label="External random clip source">
            <div class="clip-source-copy">
                <p class="eyebrow">External clip source</p>
                <strong>Drag a clip to the timeline</strong>
                <span>Two generated clips are always ready below. Drop one into a compatible track to choose its position; a new clip replaces it immediately.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="clip-source-actions">
                <div id="generated-clip-sources" class="generated-clip-sources" aria-label="Generated clips"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <lgs1920-timeline id="studio-timeline" class="demo-studio-timeline" aria-label="Studio style interactive timeline">
            <span slot="custom-menu" class="demo-skip-controls" aria-label="Ten second seek controls">
                <wa-button id="studio-seek-backward" appearance="plain" variant="brand" size="s" aria-label="Back 10 seconds" title="Back 10 seconds">
                    <wa-icon slot="start" name="arrow-rotate-left" variant="solid" aria-hidden="true"></wa-icon>
                    -10s
                </wa-button>
                <wa-button id="studio-seek-forward" appearance="plain" variant="brand" size="s" aria-label="Forward 10 seconds" title="Forward 10 seconds">
                    <wa-icon slot="start" name="arrow-rotate-right" variant="solid" aria-hidden="true"></wa-icon>
                    +10s
                </wa-button>
            </span>
            <span slot="overlay-text">Preparing timeline...</span>
        </lgs1920-timeline>
        <div class="timeline-output">
            <span>Last event</span>
            <code id="studio-output">None</code>
        </div>
        <wa-toast id="studio-toast" placement="bottom-end"></wa-toast>
        <div class="demo-explanation">
            <article>
                <p class="eyebrow">What to observe</p>
            <p>The host receives <code>seek</code> intent and writes <code>event.detail.timeMillis</code> back to the component. It also owns the playback clock: <code>play</code> starts it, <code>pause</code> stops it, and each frame updates <code>currentTimeMillis</code>. The standard time and zoom controls stay inside the component. The top menu slot contains the 10-second rewind and advance buttons. The clip sources are outside the custom element, so they can live in a toolbar, palette, or application menu. Two randomized clips are always available for dragging, and each accepted drop replaces its source with a new one.</p>
            </article>
            <pre><code data-language="mixed">&lt;lgs1920-timeline&gt;
    &lt;span slot="custom-menu"&gt;
        &lt;wa-button appearance="plain" variant="brand" size="s" aria-label="Back 10 seconds"&gt;&lt;wa-icon slot="start" name="arrow-rotate-left" variant="solid"&gt;&lt;/wa-icon&gt;-10s&lt;/wa-button&gt;
        &lt;wa-button appearance="plain" variant="brand" size="s" aria-label="Forward 10 seconds"&gt;&lt;wa-icon slot="start" name="arrow-rotate-right" variant="solid"&gt;&lt;/wa-icon&gt;+10s&lt;/wa-button&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/lgs1920-timeline&gt;

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-seek', event =&gt; {
    clock.seek(event.detail.timeMillis)
})

&lt;p&gt;Drag a clip to the timeline&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id="generated-clip-sources"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
            <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-play', () =&gt; {
    timeline.playing = true
    clock.start()
})

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-pause', () =&gt; {
    timeline.playing = false
    clock.stop()
})

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-seek', event =&gt; {
    timeline.currentTimeMillis = event.detail.timeMillis
    clock.seek(event.detail.timeMillis)
})</code></pre>
            <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">import {CLIP_OPTION_DRAG_MIME} from '@lgs1920/timeline'

const clipSources = document.querySelector('#generated-clip-sources')
const replenishClipSources = () =&gt; {
    while (clipSources.children.length &lt; 2) {
    const option = createRandomClipOption()
    const clip = document.createElement('wa-button')
    clip.textContent = `${option.label} · ${option.duration}s`
    clip.draggable = true
    clip.addEventListener('dragstart', event =&gt; {
        event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'copy'
        event.dataTransfer.setData(CLIP_OPTION_DRAG_MIME, JSON.stringify(option))
    })
    clipSources.append(clip)
    }
}

replenishClipSources()
</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p id="clip-drag-status" class="demo-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">Drag one of the two clips onto the timeline. Each accepted drop creates a replacement clip.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-panel playground" aria-labelledby="interactive-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Demo 02 · Editing and events</p>
                <h2 id="interactive-title">Move clips and inspect the contract</h2>
            </div>
            <span id="event-status" class="event-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</span>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">Drag a clip, resize it, change a track label, or use the playback toolbar. The host advances the clock after a <code>play</code> event, so this demo shows the same integration pattern as the Studio example. Every interaction emits a namespaced event; this demo writes accepted track changes back to the element.</p>
        <lgs1920-timeline id="interactive-timeline" aria-label="Interactive editing timeline"></lgs1920-timeline>
        <div class="timeline-output demo02-event-output">
            <div class="demo02-event-controls">
                <span>Last event</span>
            </div>
            <code id="event-output">None</code>
        </div>
        <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-clip-change', event =&gt; {
    timeline.tracks = event.detail.tracks
})

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-seek', event =&gt; {
    timeline.currentTimeMillis = event.detail.timeMillis
})</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="example-grid" aria-label="Timeline examples">
        <article class="demo-panel example-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Demo 03 · Read only</p>
            <h2>Mirror an external player</h2>
            <p>The timeline is a read-only projection: an external player owns the controls and sends its current time to the component. Use this pattern for a video player, a presentation preview, or a monitoring screen.</p>
            <div class="readonly-controls">
                <wa-button id="readonly-play" appearance="accent" size="s">Play preview</wa-button>
                <wa-slider id="readonly-time-slider" label="External player time" size="s" variant="brand" with-tooltip min="0" max="30000" step="33.333" value="0"></wa-slider>
            </div>
            <lgs1920-timeline id="readonly-timeline" aria-label="Read only timeline"></lgs1920-timeline>
            <p id="readonly-status" class="demo-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">External player paused · 00:00</p>
            <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">timeline.timeline = {
    interactive: false,
    editable: false,
}

player.addEventListener('timeupdate', event =&gt; {
    timeline.currentTimeMillis = event.detail.timeMillis
})
</code></pre>
        </article>
        <article class="demo-panel example-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Demo 04 · Video range</p>
            <h2>Limit playback to a selected range</h2>
            <p>Drag the colored start and end handles on the ruler. The playback clock stops at the selected end, which is useful when the timeline represents an in and out range. Keyboard users can focus the handles and move them with the arrow keys.</p>
            <wa-slider id="range-time-slider" label="Range playback time" size="s" variant="brand" with-tooltip min="0" max="30000" step="33.333" value="0"></wa-slider>
            <lgs1920-timeline id="range-timeline" aria-label="Timeline with editable video range"></lgs1920-timeline>
            <p id="range-status" class="demo-note" role="status" aria-live="polite">Range: 00:06 – 00:24 · Playback paused at 00:06</p>
            <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">timeline.timeline = {
    rangeStartMillis: 6_000,
    rangeEndMillis: 24_000,
}

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-range-change', event =&gt; {
    console.log(event.detail.startMillis, event.detail.endMillis)
})</code></pre>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-panel api-demo" aria-labelledby="slots-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Demo 05 · Slots and controlled state</p>
        <h2 id="slots-title">Compose the surrounding UI</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">The component owns the timeline surface while the application owns its context: a time slider in <code>timeline-ruler</code>, a zoom control in <code>timeline-controls</code>, and application actions in <code>custom-menu</code>. The full slot reference is available in the documentation.</p>
        <div class="slot-list" aria-label="Slots used in the demos">
            <span class="demo-slot-chip">timeline-ruler · external scrubber</span>
            <span class="demo-slot-chip">timeline-controls · horizontal zoom</span>
            <span class="demo-slot-chip">custom-menu · host actions</span>
            <span class="demo-slot-chip">overlay-text · initial loading label</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="html">&lt;lgs1920-timeline&gt;
    &lt;span slot="timeline-ruler"&gt;...time slider...&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span slot="timeline-controls"&gt;...zoom slider...&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;wa-button slot="custom-menu"&gt;Settings&lt;/wa-button&gt;
&lt;/lgs1920-timeline&gt;</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-panel api-demo keyboard-reference" aria-labelledby="keyboard-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Demo 06 · Keyboard shortcuts</p>
        <h2 id="keyboard-title">Keep editing within reach of the keyboard</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">Focus the timeline surface, a range handle, a clip, a clip resize handle, or the legend divider, then use the matching shortcuts below. The live status line records the last key pressed inside the Studio-style timeline.</p>
        <p id="keyboard-status" class="keyboard-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Click the Studio timeline, then press a shortcut.</p>
        <div class="keyboard-table-wrap">
            <table class="keyboard-table">
                <caption>Timeline keyboard shortcuts</caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Focus or context</th>
                        <th scope="col">Keys</th>
                        <th scope="col">Action</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Toggle local playback.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>Home</kbd> · <kbd>End</kbd></td><td>Move the playhead to the selected range start or end.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move the playhead to the selected range boundary.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>↑</kbd> / <kbd>↓</kbd></td><td>Scroll tracks to the top or bottom.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>↑</kbd> / <kbd>↓</kbd></td><td>Increase or decrease row height.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Timeline surface</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Zoom the ruler horizontally when no clip is selected.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Scrollbar rail</th><td><kbd>PageUp</kbd> · <kbd>PageDown</kbd> · arrows</td><td>Scroll one viewport in the focused direction.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Playhead grip</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move by <code>keyboardStepSeconds</code>.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Playhead grip</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move by ten keyboard steps.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Playhead grip</th><td><kbd>Alt</kbd> + <kbd>→</kbd> / <kbd>←</kbd></td><td>Jump to the range minimum or maximum.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Range handle</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move the focused boundary by one keyboard step.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Range handle</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move the focused boundary by ten keyboard steps.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move the selected clip by one rendered pixel.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>Alt</kbd> + <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Move the selected clip by ten rendered pixels.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>Delete</kbd> · <kbd>Backspace</kbd></td><td>Delete the focused editable clip.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>Mod</kbd> + <kbd>C</kbd></td><td>Start a copy placement ghost; click to place it.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>Mod</kbd> + <kbd>D</kbd></td><td>Duplicate the clip immediately after itself.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>M</kbd></td><td>Mask or reveal the clip.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip</th><td><kbd>V</kbd></td><td>Enable or disable the clip.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Non-movable clip</th><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> · <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Select the clip.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip resize handle</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Resize the focused edge by one keyboard step.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Clip resize handle</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Resize the focused edge by ten keyboard steps.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Any active edit</th><td><kbd>Escape</kbd></td><td>Cancel a copy, drag, resize, or context menu; clear clip selection.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Legend divider</th><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd></td><td>Resize the track legend.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Legend divider</th><td><kbd>Shift</kbd> + arrows · <kbd>Home</kbd> · <kbd>End</kbd> · <kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Change the resize step, select the minimum or maximum, or collapse and restore the legend.</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Track label editor</th><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> · <kbd>Escape</kbd></td><td>Commit or cancel the label edit.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="keyboard-note"><strong>Mod</strong> means <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> on Windows and Linux, and <kbd>⌘</kbd> on macOS. Wheel gestures are also available on the timeline surface: <kbd>Shift</kbd> or <kbd>Alt</kbd> + wheel changes row height, while <kbd>Meta</kbd> + wheel changes horizontal ruler zoom. <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + wheel remains available to the browser.</p>
        <pre class="demo-code"><code data-language="javascript">timeline.timeline = {
    keyboardZoomActive: true,
    keyboardStepSeconds: 0.1,
}

timeline.addEventListener('lgs1920-timeline-seek', event =&gt; {
    timeline.currentTimeMillis = event.detail.timeMillis
})

// The component handles the shortcuts according to the focused part.
// The host only needs to keep controlled state synchronized.</code></pre>
    </section>
</main>
<script type="module" src="./assets/app.bundle.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
